class.description:
Streaming assets are files that ship with a game unchanged, outside the import pipeline: videos, large audio files, configuration files, data for native libraries or files that players may replace (mods). They live in one folder of the project, [member ProjectSettings.filesystem/streaming_assets/source_folder], and are turned on with [member ProjectSettings.filesystem/streaming_assets/enabled].
[StreamingAssetsServer] owns these project settings and the locked [code]streaming://[/code] path prefix of [PathPrefixServer]. Once at startup, after the project settings and the main pack are loaded, it finds where the files are on this run (see [enum Location]) and points [code]streaming://[/code] there:
- in the editor and in games run from the editor: the source folder of the project ([constant LOCATION_SOURCE_FOLDER]);
- in [code]Raw[/code] mode on Windows and Linux: the folder [member ProjectSettings.filesystem/streaming_assets/target_folder] next to the executable ([constant LOCATION_EXTERNAL_FOLDER]);
- in [code]Raw[/code] mode on macOS and iOS: the same folder inside the bundle resources ([constant LOCATION_BUNDLE]);
- in [code]Pack[/code] mode: the streaming pack [member ProjectSettings.filesystem/streaming_assets/pack_file] next to the main pack, which is mounted at startup ([constant LOCATION_PACK]);
- otherwise, with the [code]Embed[/code] fallback (Android, the Web): the copy of the folder inside the main pack ([constant LOCATION_EMBEDDED]).
Games read the files the same way on every platform, with [FileAccess], [DirAccess] and the runtime loaders:
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var file = FileAccess.open("streaming://config/levels.json", FileAccess.READ)
var levels = JSON.parse_string(file.get_as_text())
var image = Image.load_from_file("streaming://textures/skybox.png")
print(StreamingAssetsServer.get_location())
# An OS path for native libraries, or "" if the files are inside a pack.
print(StreamingAssetsServer.get_os_path("streaming://video/intro.ogv"))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
using var file = FileAccess.Open("streaming://config/levels.json", FileAccess.ModeFlags.Read);
var levels = Json.ParseString(file.GetAsText());
var image = Image.LoadFromFile("streaming://textures/skybox.png");
GD.Print(StreamingAssetsServer.GetLocation());
// An OS path for native libraries, or "" if the files are inside a pack.
GD.Print(StreamingAssetsServer.GetOsPath("streaming://video/intro.ogv"));
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
The settings need a restart: the location is resolved once. Debug builds and the editor accept the command line argument [code]--streaming-assets-path=<folder>[/code], which forces [constant LOCATION_EXTERNAL_FOLDER] with that folder, for example to test the layout of an export.
[b]Note:[/b] [code]streaming://[/code] is read-only except for the source folder in the editor. It can't be replaced or removed with [method PathPrefixServer.register_prefix] or [method PathPrefixServer.unregister_prefix].
